    {
      "unit_id": "tag:08WU:proof",
      "source_text": "By (<REF_0001>), for any <MATH_0001> we have a \ncommutative diagram\n<MATH_0002>\nIf <MATH_0003> is universally injective, then <MATH_0004> is injective,\nso both rows in the above diagram are surjective for <MATH_0005>. We may thus \nlift\n<MATH_0006> to some <MATH_0007> splitting \n<MATH_0008>.\nConversely, if <MATH_0009> is a split surjection, then \nboth rows in the above diagram are surjective,\nso by Lemma <REF_0002>, <MATH_0010> is injective.\n",
