      "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\nAny functor <MATH_0001> of abelian categories\nwhich is exact and takes nonzero objects to nonzero objects reflects\ninjections and surjections. Namely, exactness implies that\n<MATH_0002> preserves kernels and cokernels (compare with\nHomology, Section <REF_0001>).\nFor example, if <MATH_0003> is a \nfaithfully flat ring homomorphism, then\n<MATH_0004> has these properties.\n<STRUCT_0002>",
